{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"GHSA-wm3x-v3qw-4jh3","published":"2026-11-12T23:37:09Z","modified":"2026-11-12T23:45:03.300210592Z","aliases":["CVE-2026-126081"],"summary":"Action Pack: Possible Strong Parameters Bypass in Parameters#each_key","details":"### Impact\n`ActionController::Parameters#each_key` delegates to the internal `ActiveSupport::HashWithIndifferentAccess` that holds the request parameters, so when called with a block it returns that hash instead of the `Parameters` instance. The hash does not respond to `permitted?`, so Active Model mass assignment (`new`, `assign_attributes`, `update`) accepts it without raising `ActiveModel::ForbiddenAttributesError`. An application that passes the return value of `each_key` to mass assignment could allow a remote, unauthenticated attacker to set attributes that the application does not permit, such as an authorization flag.\n\nThis is an incomplete fix of [CVE-2020-8164](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-8727-m6gj-mc37), which made `each`, `each_pair` and `each_value` return the `Parameters` instance but left `each_key` delegated.\n\n### Details\nThe fixed releases define `Parameters#each_key` to yield each key and return the `Parameters` instance when given a block, as `each`, `each_pair` and `each_value` do, and to return an `Enumerator` without one. Code that used the return value of `each_key` as a hash now receives the `Parameters` instance, which mass assignment rejects unless it is permitted.\n\n### Affected applications\nAn application is affected if it passes the return value of `ActionController::Parameters#each_key`, called with a block, to mass assignment. Rails itself makes no such call.\n\n### Workarounds\nDo not use the return value of `each_key`. Call it for its block only, and pass the permitted `Parameters` instance to mass assignment.\n\n### Releases\nThe fixed releases are available at the normal locations.\n\nPatches for those who cannot upgrade at once:\n- 8.1: https://github.com/rails/rails/commit/8ba746e0a786458c281060823f2ccc5c5f6312ac.patch\n- 8.0: https://github.com/rails/rails/commit/2fc8838300133931e19eed3ea6cee76a7e83f19c.patch\n\n### Versions affected\n- actionpack < 8.0.5.2\n- actionpack >= 8.1, < 8.1.4.1\n\n### Credit\nThis issue was responsibly reported by HackerOne researcher [smlee](https://hackerone.com/smlee).","affected":[{"package":{"name":"actionpack","ecosystem":"RubyGems","purl":"pkg:gem/actionpack"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"8.1.0.beta1"},{"fixed":"8.1.4.1"}]}],"versions":["8.1.0","8.1.0.beta1","8.1.0.rc1","8.1.1","8.1.2","8.1.2.1","8.1.3","8.1.3.1","8.1.4"],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/advisories/github-reviewed/2026/11/GHSA-wm3x-v3qw-4jh3/GHSA-wm3x-v3qw-4jh3.json"}},{"package":{"name":"actionpack","ecosystem":"RubyGems","purl":"pkg:gem/actionpack"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"8.0.5.2"}]}],"versions":["0.9.0","0.9.5","1.0.0","1.0.1","1.1.0","1.10.1","1.10.2","1.11.0","1.11.1","1.11.2","1.12.0","1.12.1","1.12.2","1.12.3","1.12.4","1.12.5","1.13.0","1.13.1","1.13.2","1.13.3","1.13.4","1.13.5","1.13.6","1.2.0","1.3.0","1.3.1","1.4.0","1.5.0","1.5.1","1.6.0","1.7.0","1.8.0","1.8.1","1.9.0","1.9.1","2.0.0","2.0.1","2.0.2","2.0.4","2.0.5","2.1.0","2.1.1","2.1.2","2.2.2","2.2.3","2.3.10","2.3.11","2.3.12","2.3.14","2.3.15","2.3.16","2.3.17","2.3.18","2.3.2","2.3.3","2.3.4","2.3.5","2.3.6","2.3.7","2.3.8","2.3.8.pre1","2.3.9","2.3.9.pre","3.0.0","3.0.0.beta","3.0.0.beta2","3.0.0.beta3","3.0.0.beta4","3.0.0.rc","3.0.0.rc2","3.0.1","3.0.10","3.0.10.rc1","3.0.11","3.0.12","3.0.12.rc1","3.0.13","3.0.13.rc1","3.0.14","3.0.15","3.0.16","3.0.17","3.0.18","3.0.19","3.0.2","3.0.20","3.0.3","3.0.4","3.0.4.rc1","3.0.5","3.0.5.rc1","3.0.6","3.0.6.rc1","3.0.6.rc2","3.0.7","3.0.7.rc1","3.0.7.rc2","3.0.8","3.0.8.rc1","3.0.8.rc2","3.0.8.rc4","3.0.9","3.0.9.rc1","3.0.9.rc3","3.0.9.rc4","3.0.9.rc5","3.1.0","3.1.0.beta1","3.1.0.rc